{"kind":"assert","text":"Static advisory for the existing live-site design, e380eda6 / plan020 at 400986e2. I read the complete plan and freshly checked official Cloudflare documentation; no provider operations, tool installation or source execution.\n\nDistinguish the provider's two preview mechanisms before promising exact promotion. Version URLs execute an uploaded version with that version's production resources; they do not create isolated branch resources. Cloudflare's newer Previews give branch environments their own configuration, with automatic Durable Object/container isolation and separately configured KV/D1/R2 resources; service bindings still call the target Worker's production deployment. Sources: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/previews/compare-workflows/ and https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/previews/ (checked 2026-10-05).\n\nA Preview's branch URL is mutable, while its deployment URL identifies one deployment. Previews have bounded provider retention (100/500 previews per Worker by plan, 100 deployments per preview) and delete the oldest automatically at capacity. Therefore a recorded URI/URL alone does not establish continued replayable artifact availability or recovery custody. Design the retained build digest, immutable deployment identity, preview-to-production configuration/resource boundary, and retention/recreation obligations; do not assume the branch alias is the reviewed version. Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/previews/.\n\nRollback creates a new deployment of a prior version, but does not revert connected resource data. Official documentation limits rollback to the most recent 100 published versions and identifies resource/class lifecycle changes that can prevent it. Thus immediate rollback should have explicit eligibility and preserved version/resource requirements, plus ordinary refused/unknown attempt ownership and recovery, rather than an unconditional promise from immutable code alone. Source: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/versions-and-deployments/rollbacks/.\n\nInference for the design owner, not an implemented finding: choose and record which provider mechanism constitutes a lane preview; state whether exact promotion means the same artifact bytes or the same provider version/configuration; keep review, grant, effect identity, lost-response recovery, signed rollback and all five capacity dimensions connected. The existing request owns these joins; no separate feature scope or narrowed acceptance story is proposed.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","scope":"Primary-document advisory for existing repository-to-live-site design request; no implementation, provider execution, adoption or source acceptance."}}